+
+## Developer diagnostics
+
+The homepage includes independent hardware (private LAN IPv4) and companion CLI
+(loopback) connection cards. The editable defaults are
+`http://192.168.1.100:8080/api/status` and
+`http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/status`; replace these with the endpoints your services
+actually expose. The widget does not install or start a companion service.
+
+Each Connect action makes a browser-side CORS GET request with
+`targetAddressSpace: 'local'` for hardware or `'loopback'` for the CLI. No server
+proxy or automatic discovery is involved. Use HTTPS for the site (localhost is
+also suitable for development), a browser supporting Local Network Access, and
+allow the appropriate network permission when prompted. See the
+[Chrome Local Network Access guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access).
+
+Services must return a successful HTTP status and allow the page's origin with
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. Requests omit credentials and reject redirects.
+Hardware should listen on its LAN interface, while the CLI should listen on
+loopback. JSON and plain text responses are supported; the displayed response is
+limited to 16 KiB. Each check times out after 10 seconds and can be cancelled.
+“Reachable” describes a completed check, not a persistent connection; use Check
+again to refresh it.
